    "snowbird": {
      "status": "ok",
      "resort": "Snowbird",
      "adapter": "powdr",
      "updatedAt": "2026-04-07 16:40:00",
      "note": "Howdy and good morning! This is Kolton with your Snow Report for Tuesday, April 7. It's going to be another warm and sunny day up at Snowbird, so make sure to layer on the sunscreen. Today's forecast calls for highs near 56 with West winds between 6 and 10 mph. With spring temps, my recommendation is to start your morning off back in Mineral Basin where the groomers will be ripping and the corn and slush skiing will arrive first. Make your journey over to the Peruvian-side or Gad-side around 11 am to Noon. Lastly, if the legs are still feeling strong, save the best for last, as late afternoon is when Road to Provo and Regulator find their prime spring skiing conditions off of the Little Cloud lift. That is how i'll be spending my day, and if it doesn't make for your perfect Bird day, feel free to blame our other Snow Reporter, Owen. Some upcoming events to keep on your radar: the U.S. Ski Hall of Fame starts this Friday & Saturday! Follow that up with the Blister Summit runs all of next week, with demos full of next season's gear, giveaways and more, but you've got to sign up , so don't forget. Just a friendly reminder: Chickadee Bowl is closed for construction as we begin upgrading Chickadee Lift into a 4-seater. If you're parking in Entry 4, your easiest mountain access will be via Who Dunnit/Creekside Road alongside the Bypass parking lot. Join us for another groovy time during Snowbird's spring Surf Season! #GMTB",
      "metrics": {
        "snow24h": 0,
